      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Performing a separate `DfuGetStatus()` and `sleep_()` here before calling `DfuPollIdle()` introduces a few issues:\n\n1. **Exceeds `kUsbDfuTimeout` and duplicates sleep clamping:** The initial `sleep_()` at lines 392–393 is not counted toward `DfuPollIdle()`\u0027s `slept \u003c kUsbDfuTimeout` loop. If a device stays busy, recovery can sleep for `first_poll_timeout + kUsbDfuTimeout` (up to `2 * kUsbDfuTimeout` \u003d 120s, or 85s in `TimesOutWhenDeviceStaysBusy` instead of clamping the total wait to 60s).\n2. **Sleeps on unexpected non-busy states and ignores `bStatus`:** Checking `settled !\u003d DfuState::kDfuIdle \u0026\u0026 settled !\u003d DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle` treats unexpected non-busy states (such as `kDfuManifestWaitReset`) as busy—sleeping for `poll_timeout` and issuing a second `DfuGetStatus()` before `DfuPollIdle()` rejects them—while ignoring `status-\u003estatus !\u003d DfuStatus::kOk` when `state` is `kDfuIdle`, `kDfuDnloadIdle`, or `kDfuUploadIdle`.\n3. **Does not recover if a busy state settles into `dfuERROR`, and splits the `kAbort` branch:** If an interrupted busy operation finishes in `kDfuError`, `DfuPollIdle()` fails with `RtsError::kDeviceRejected` instead of clearing it with `DFU_CLRSTATUS`. Polling while busy first also lets `kDfuDnloadIdle` and `kDfuUploadIdle` share a single `DfuRequest::kAbort` branch.\n\nConsider extracting a `DfuPollSettled(int interface)` helper (declared in `rts5817_usb_device.h`) that polls `DfuGetStatus()` while the device reports a transient busy state (`kDfuDnloadSync`, `kDfuDnloadBusy`, `kDfuManifestSync`, `kDfuManifest` with `DfuStatus::kOk`), and calling it from both `DfuPollIdle()` and `DfuRecoverToIdle()`:\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cDfuStatusResponse, RtsError\u003e RtsUsbDevice::DfuPollSettled(\n    int interface) {\n  using enum DfuState;\n\n  // Bound the whole wait: the manifest phase (flash programming and image\n  // verification) can take tens of seconds.\n  std::chrono::milliseconds slept{0};\n\n  while (slept \u003c kUsbDfuTimeout) {\n    auto status \u003d DfuGetStatus(interface);\n    if (!status) {\n      return std::unexpected(status.error());\n    }\n\n    if (status-\u003estatus !\u003d DfuStatus::kOk ||\n        (status-\u003estate !\u003d kDfuDnloadSync \u0026\u0026 status-\u003estate !\u003d kDfuDnloadBusy \u0026\u0026\n         status-\u003estate !\u003d kDfuManifestSync \u0026\u0026 status-\u003estate !\u003d kDfuManifest)) {\n      return *status;\n    }\n\n    // Never sleep past the overall timeout.\n    const auto delay \u003d\n        std::min(std::max(status-\u003epoll_timeout, kDfuMinPollDelay),\n                 kUsbDfuTimeout - slept);\n\n    sleep_(delay);\n    slept +\u003d delay;\n  }\n\n  std::println(stderr, \"Timed out waiting for DFU idle state.\");\n  return std::unexpected(RtsError::kTimeout);\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cDfuState, RtsError\u003e RtsUsbDevice::DfuPollIdle(int interface) {\n  auto status \u003d DfuPollSettled(interface);\n  if (!status) {\n    return std::unexpected(status.error());\n  }\n\n  if (status-\u003estatus !\u003d DfuStatus::kOk ||\n      status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuError) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"DFU error: bStatus\u003d{}, bState\u003d{}\",\n                 std::to_underlying(status-\u003estatus),\n                 std::to_underlying(status-\u003estate));\n    return std::unexpected(RtsError::kDeviceRejected);\n  }\n\n  if (status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuIdle ||\n      status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle) {\n    return status-\u003estate;\n  }\n\n  std::println(stderr, \"Unexpected DFU state: bState\u003d{}\",\n               std::to_underlying(status-\u003estate));\n  return std::unexpected(RtsError::kProtocolError);\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, RtsError\u003e RtsUsbDevice::DfuRecoverToIdle(int interface) {\n  auto status \u003d DfuPollSettled(interface);\n  if (!status) {\n    return std::unexpected(status.error());\n  }\n\n  if (status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuError) {\n    // CLRSTATUS is only valid here.\n    return DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kClrStatus, 0, interface);\n  }\n  if (status-\u003estatus !\u003d DfuStatus::kOk) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"DFU error: bStatus\u003d{}, bState\u003d{}\",\n                 std::to_underlying(status-\u003estatus),\n                 std::to_underlying(status-\u003estate));\n    return std::unexpected(RtsError::kDeviceRejected);\n  }\n\n  switch (status-\u003estate) {\n    case DfuState::kDfuIdle:\n      return {};\n    case DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle:\n    case DfuState::kDfuUploadIdle:\n      return DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kAbort, 0, interface);\n    default:\n      std::println(stderr, \"Unexpected DFU state: bState\u003d{}\",\n                   std::to_underlying(status-\u003estate));\n      return std::unexpected(RtsError::kProtocolError);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/299f4ff5-df51-438e-9ffa-b26782cf1cb6)",
